 "context": [
  {
   "h": "From Spain to Italy",
   "body": "<p>Hamilcar died in Spain in 229 or 228 BC, and command passed to his son-in-law Hasdrubal, who extended Carthaginian power and founded New Carthage (Cartagena). When Hasdrubal was murdered in 221 BC, the army chose Hannibal, and Carthage confirmed the choice.</p><p>In 219 BC Hannibal besieged Saguntum, a city on the east coast of Spain that had made friends with Rome. It fell after eight months, and Rome declared war. In 218 BC Hannibal marched out of Spain, over the Pyrenees, across southern Gaul and the Rhône, and through the Alps in late autumn, arriving in northern Italy with perhaps half the army he had started with and only a few of his elephants. Which pass he used is still argued about.</p>"
  }
